body:
opt-in telemetry (`telemetry.enabled = true`) posts a sample of failed requests, including headers. i turned it on to help with the timeout thing in #812 and then looked at what it actually sends:

{"url": "...", "status": 504, "headers": {"authorization": "Bearer fake-tok-0000tttt", "x-request-id": "7c1"}}

pretty sure you don't want to be *receiving* other people's tokens either — that's your problem now as much as mine. suggest dropping authorization/cookie/proxy-authorization when the payload is built, not filtering them on the ingest side, so the value never leaves the machine.

`blastdemo config --show --merged` output, 0.4.0rc2. note the two `retries`:

{
  "profile": "staging",
  "log_level": "info",
  "retries": 3,
