  "plugins": {
    "lanes": {"enabled": true, "source": "entry_point", "config": {"strict": false}},
    "topology": {"enabled": true, "source": "entry_point", "config": {}},
    "blastdemo": {"enabled": false, "source": "path", "config": {"bin": "/usr/local/bin/blastdemo-cli"}}
  },
  "http": {
    "base_url": "https://freight.invalid/api",
    "retries": 7,
    "backoff_s": 0.5,
    "max_delay_s": 4,
    "headers": {"user-agent": "blastdemo/0.4.0rc2"}
  },
  "report": {"format": "text", "color": "auto", "width": null},
  "_provenance": {
    "retries": ["defaults.toml:12", "~/.config/blastdemo.toml:4", "BLASTDEMO_RETRIES"],
    "http.retries": ["defaults.toml:41"],
    "timeout_s": ["defaults.toml:13"]
  }
}

so which one wins for http calls? `--retries 1` doesnt seem to change the 7. either the flag should reach `http.retries` or `--show` shouldnt print both without saying which is live.

`blastdemo migrate --dry-run=false` on a copy of our staging db. it rolls back at the end and exits 0, which is the part that worries me — nothing in the summary says it failed.

```
[migrate] target 0.4.0rc2, current 0.3.9, 4 steps
[migrate] BEGIN;
[migrate] step 1/4 lane_cache_v3
           CREATE TABLE lane_cache_new (lane TEXT PRIMARY KEY, carrier TEXT NOT NULL, legs INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, updated_at TEXT);
           INSERT INTO lane_cache_new (lane, carrier, legs, updated_at) SELECT lane, carrier, COALESCE(legs, 0), updated_at FROM lane_cache;
           -- 12481 rows
           DROP TABLE lane_cache;
           ALTER TABLE lane_cache_new RENAME TO lane_cache;
[migrate] step 2/4 drop_legacy
           DROP TABLE IF EXISTS lane_cache_old;
           DROP INDEX IF EXISTS ix_lane_cache_carrier_legacy;
           DELETE FROM meta WHERE key IN ('cache_format_v2', 'legacy_offsets');
           -- 2 rows
[migrate] step 3/4 offsets_rebuild
           CREATE TABLE offsets (lane TEXT NOT NULL, member TEXT NOT NULL, off INTEGER NOT NULL, len INTEGER NOT NULL);
           CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ix_offsets_lane_member ON offsets (lane, member);
           INSERT INTO offsets SELECT lane, 'index.jsonl', 0, 0 FROM lane_cache;
[migrate] step 4/4 constraints
           CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ix_lane_cache_lane ON lane_cache (lane);
[migrate] ERROR sqlite3.IntegrityError: UNIQUE constraint failed: lane_cache.lane
[migrate] ROLLBACK;
[migrate] done in 8.4s
$ echo $?
0
```

the duplicate is `AC-4821` twice, once with a zero-width space in it (there is another thread about those). so the data problem is ours. two things that are yours:

1. exit 0 after a rollback — our deploy script treated this as success and moved on
2. "done in 8.4s" as the last line, with the ERROR scrolled off in CI logs

would much rather it exited nonzero and said `migration rolled back` at the end.
